17:| `packages/reporting/src/xml-chars.ts` (new) | Holds the one shared XML 1.0 character rule. `xmlSafe` replaces C0 controls (except tab, LF, CR), lone surrogates, U+FFFE and U+FFFF with U+FFFD. `hasInvalidXmlChar` detects forbidden characters, raw or as character references. `assertWellFormedChars(bytes)` checks every `*.xml` and `*.rels` part of a finished OOXML package and throws a `RenderError` if one fails. |
51:**Why a corrupt file can't be stored as succeeded.** If any part of a finished package still holds a forbidden character, raw or as a reference, the renderer throws `RenderError`. The runner already maps that to `export.render_failed`: no retry, no file stored (existing path, `export-runner.ts` catch block; `exports.test.ts` covers RenderError → failed with no file). The unit test `assertWellFormedChars refuses a package holding a forbidden character` proves the check throws `RenderError`.
